;; Package abi is the guest's hypercall ABI as Go constants (doc/GUEST.md,
;; *The hypercall ABI*): the doorbell's address, the call numbers and the
;; call block's layout -- what guest/rt/rt.c spells in C for the C guest,
;; and what the Go guest (guest/tamago, built with TamaGo) imports.  It
;; imports nothing, so that a GOOS=tamago build can use it; vmm's test holds
;; the monitor's own numbers to it.
(in-ns 'go.arbace.box.abi) (go/file "abi.go" :doc "Package abi is the guest's hypercall ABI as Go constants (doc/GUEST.md,\n*The hypercall ABI*): the doorbell's address, the call numbers and the\ncall block's layout -- what guest/rt/rt.c spells in C for the C guest,\nand what the Go guest (guest/tamago, built with TamaGo) imports.  It\nimports nothing, so that a GOOS=tamago build can use it; vmm's test holds\nthe monitor's own numbers to it.\n" :imports [])




(go/const ^{:val 4026531840 :doc "Doorbell is the guest-physical address no memory backs: a guest stores\nits call block's address there, one 64-bit store (from RAX on amd64, X0\non arm64), and exits to the monitor.\n"} Doorbell 0xf0000000)






(go/const "The calls: the core's 17 host functions in doc/GUEST.md's order, the\nruntime's report of a fault, what a Go runtime asks besides (a Go\nguest's): random bytes, for its hashes' seeds; and the wait and the read\nmerged, which both guests make in place of a wait.\nAlloc and Free are answered in the guest and never made.\n"
  ^{:line 20} [^{:val 1} HostInit (+ iota 1)]
  ^{:line 21} [^{:val 2} GetWinsize]
  ^{:line 22} [^{:val 3} TermStart]
  ^{:line 23} [^{:val 4} TermStop]
  ^{:line 24} [^{:val 5} TTYKeys]
  ^{:line 25} [^{:val 6} NowMs]
  ^{:line 26} [^{:val 7} Delay]
  ^{:line 27} [^{:val 8} WaitForInput]
  ^{:line 28} [^{:val 9} ReadInput]
  ^{:line 29} [^{:val 10} Suspend]
  ^{:line 30} [^{:val 11} Exit]
  ^{:line 31} [^{:val 12} Message]
  ^{:line 32} [^{:val 13} Alloc]
  ^{:line 33} [^{:val 14} Free]
  ^{:line 34} [^{:val 15} Write]
  ^{:line 35} [^{:val 16} Time]
  ^{:line 36} [^{:val 17} Raise]
  ^{:line 37} [^{:val 18} Fault]
  ^{:line 38} [^{:val 19} Random] ; a[0] a buffer, a[1] its length: filled with random bytes





  ^{:line 44} [^{:val 20 :doc "WaitRead is wait_for_input and read_input merged (doc/GUEST.md, *The\nmerged wait and read*): a[0] the wait's ms, a[1] a buffer, a[2] its\nlength.  The monitor waits; when there is input, it reads into the\nbuffer at once.  ret is the wait's answer, and when it is 1, a[0] the\nread's: the count, 0 at the end, -1 for a signal.\n"} WaitRead]












  ^{:line 57} [^{:val 21 :doc "The calls of a Go guest on several vCPUs (doc/GUEST.md, *SMP*): the\nruntime's goos.Task, Idle, Wake and ProcID, which TamaGo's own boards\nanswer with an IPI and a halt, answered by the monitor.  None is a\nhost function: they are not serialised with the others.\n\nCPUStart starts vCPU a[0] (1 to the count less one), idle since the\nboot, at the image's whim_apentry: a[1] its stack, a[2] the M's g0,\na[3] the function it calls (the runtime's mstart).  a[4] is the top\nof the TaskStackBytes the runtime allocated for the M's stack, which\nthe board does not use (its g0's own is a[1]): the monitor gives\ntheir pages back to the host.  ret is 0, or -1 when that vCPU does\nnot exist or has started already.\n"} CPUStart]




  ^{:line 62} [^{:val 22 :doc "CPUPark stops the calling vCPU until a CPUWake names it, a[0]\nnanoseconds pass (a[0] < 0: no limit of the guest's), or the monitor\nlets it look again (doc/GUEST.md, *SMP*: no longer than a\nmillisecond while another vCPU runs the guest).\n"} CPUPark]


  ^{:line 65} [^{:val 23 :doc "CPUWake ends vCPU a[0]'s park, or its next one when it is not parked;\na[0] = -1: every vCPU's but the caller's.\n"} CPUWake]

  ^{:line 67} [^{:val 24 :doc "CPUSelf is the calling vCPU's number, in ret: 0 the boot vCPU.\n"} CPUSelf]










  ^{:line 78} [^{:val 25 :doc "The store (doc/LISP-SANDBOX.md, *The store*): the box's data, kept by\nthe monitor in a directory of the host's it is given\n(WHIM_GUEST_STORE), so that no data need be built into an image.\nBlobs are immutable and named by their SHA-256; refs are names a\nguest gives a blob, the store's only mutable state.  Not host\nfunctions: answered by the monitor, not serialised with the others.\nWithout a store every call answers -1.\n\nBlobPut stores a[1] bytes at a[0] and writes their SHA-256 to the 32\nbytes at a[2]: ret 0, or -1.\n"} BlobPut]


  ^{:line 81} [^{:val 26 :doc "BlobSize is the size of the blob whose hash is the 32 bytes at a[0],\nin ret, or -1 when the store has none.\n"} BlobSize]


  ^{:line 84} [^{:val 27 :doc "BlobGet reads the blob whose hash is at a[0] from offset a[3] into\na[2] bytes at a[1]: ret the count (0 past its end), or -1.\n"} BlobGet]


  ^{:line 87} [^{:val 28 :doc "RefGet writes the hash ref a[0]'s a[1] bytes name to the 32 bytes at\na[2]: ret 0, or -1 when there is no such ref.\n"} RefGet]





  ^{:line 93} [^{:val 29 :doc "RefSet points ref a[0] (a[1] bytes) at the hash at a[2] -- a blob the\nstore has -- when a[3] is 0, or when the ref's hash is the 32 bytes\nat a[3] (compare and set; all zero: the ref must not exist): ret 0,\n-1 for a name or hash it refuses, -2 when the comparison failed.  A\nname is 1 to 64 of [A-Za-z0-9._-], not beginning with a dot.\n"} RefSet]
  ^{:line 94} [^{:val 30} NCalls])




